	"_comment": "Shared cross-evaluator fixture matrix for the directory-exclude feature. Consumed by src/shared/exclude-rules.test.ts (the TypeScript evaluator's own tests) and, unchanged, by the sh and PowerShell parity runners. `dedicated: true` means this case's real behavior is asserted by a dedicated test elsewhere (it needs on-disk construction a declarative row can't express — a symlink, a hardlink, a specific permission bit, a case-variant real directory, or a Windows ACL); this row only satisfies the by-name existence/floor check. A home/cwd/rulesFileLines value on a dedicated row is documentation of intent, not literal input to any generic loop.",
